  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses solely on the product of the maximum outcome and its probability, which is distinct from expected value (which sums all outcome-probability products). The individual, however, explicitly refers to computing the full expected value for each lottery, which involves summing all (outcome × probability) pairs, not just focusing on the maximum outcome. This indicates a different decision rule. The information considered by the individual (all outcomes and probabilities) goes beyond what is required by the decision reason (only maximum outcome and its probability). Furthermore, the justification based on expected value does not align with the rule of comparing maximum outcome-probability products. Therefore, the individual did not use the specified decision reason.",
